# Work case study links (live vs Wayback)

## Rule of thumb

If a case study has a `waybackUrl`, the **live site is no longer (or not only) the design in the case study**. Do **not** hide the live link — show both, and always attach a `liveLinkNote` disclaimer when `liveLink` is also present.

## Frontmatter

| Field | When |
|-------|------|
| `waybackUrl` | Archive / staging / Webflow URL that shows **this** case study’s design |
| `liveLink` | Current public URL (optional; keep when useful) |
| `liveLinkNote` | **Required** whenever both `liveLink` and `waybackUrl` are set |
| `proposalLink` | Unaccepted / alternate direction prototype (optional) |
| `proposalLinkLabel` | Pill label for `proposalLink` (default in UI: `Proposed redesign`) |

Example (site replaced; live is not your design):

```yaml
liveLink: "https://example.org"
liveLinkNote: "The live site is a different design and was not designed by me. Use the Wayback Machine link to see this work."
waybackUrl: "https://web.archive.org/web/.../https://example.webflow.io/"
```

Example (your redesign is live; Wayback is a prior version):

```yaml
liveLink: "https://example.com"
liveLinkNote: "The live site is the current redesign. Wayback Machine shows the prior version."
waybackUrl: "https://web.archive.org/web/.../https://www.example.com/"
```

Example (proposal not accepted; live differs from case study):

```yaml
liveLink: "https://example.org"
liveLinkNote: "The live site is a different design and was not designed by me. Wayback Machine shows the shipped work. Proposed redesign was not accepted."
waybackUrl: "https://web.archive.org/web/.../https://example.webflow.io/"
proposalLink: "https://example.netlify.app/"
proposalLinkLabel: "Proposed redesign"
```

## Wayback only

If there is no useful live URL (defunct product, acquired, etc.), set `waybackUrl` alone and omit `liveLink` / `liveLinkNote`.

## UI

Work detail pages render pills in this order: Wayback → Proposed redesign → Live → Partner case study, then `liveLinkNote` under the pills. Schema enforces the note when both live and Wayback URLs are set.
